    "bodies": [
      "Document 1:\nTitle: Closeburn Castle\nCloseburn Castle is a tower house, probably of the 14th century, but possibly older, and is one of the oldest continually inhabited houses in Scotland.  The castle is located 1 km east of the village of Closeburn, and 2 km south-east of Thornhill, in Dumfries and Galloway, south-west Scotland.\n\n",
      "Document 2:\nTitle: Roger de Kirkpatrick\nSir Roger de Kirkpatrick of Closeburn (fl.  14th century) was a Scottish gentleman, a 3rd cousin and associate of Robert the Bruce, and a 1st cousin of Sir William Wallace.  He was born circa 1280 at the Kirkpatrick stronghold of Closeburn Castle.\n\n"
